From: Spencer Bull <spencer@omarchy.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rt1320-sdw: sync regcache on SoundWire attach

rt1320_sdw_init() puts both regmap and mbq_regmap into cache-only mode
before the SoundWire peripheral attaches. On systems where the ALSA card
registers and userspace (such as UCM/alsactl) restores mixer controls
before rt1320_io_init() runs (observed on boot on the Dell XPS 16
DX16263, where pre-attach control writes log "Unknown device ID 0"),
writes to cached controls such as "RX Channel Select" (0x41080200) land
in regcache with cache_dirty set.

rt1320_io_init() clears cache_only and, on re-attach after a bus reset
(first_hw_init == true), marks both regmaps dirty without calling
regcache_sync(). Cached writes therefore stay out of sync with hardware
until a later PM runtime suspend/resume cycle runs regcache_sync().

Call regcache_sync() on both regmap and mbq_regmap in rt1320_io_init()
before marking hw_init complete, leaving the cache dirty on error so a
subsequent resume can retry, and defer scheduling load_dspfw_work until
after regcache_sync() and hw_init = true so firmware reload cannot race
against the sync on active re-attach.

Signed-off-by: Spencer Bull <spencer@omarchy.org>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/rt1320-sdw.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/rt1320-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/rt1320-sdw.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rt1320-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rt1320-sdw.c
@@ -2420,6 +2420,8 @@
 {
 	struct rt1320_sdw_priv *rt1320 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	unsigned int amp_func_status, val, tmp;
+	bool reload_dspfw = false;
+	int ret;
 
 	if (rt1320->hw_init)
 		return 0;
@@ -2491,7 +2493,7 @@
 
 		/* reload DSP FW */
 		if (rt1320->fw_load_done)
-			schedule_work(&rt1320->load_dspfw_work);
+			reload_dspfw = true;
 	}
 	if (!rt1320->first_hw_init && rt1320->version_id == RT1320_VA && rt1320->dev_id == RT1320_DEV_ID) {
 		regmap_write(rt1320->regmap, SDW_SDCA_CTL(FUNC_NUM_AMP, RT1320_SDCA_ENT_PDE23,
@@ -2522,10 +2524,22 @@
 		regcache_mark_dirty(rt1320->mbq_regmap);
 	}
 
+	/* Flush early pre-attach writes and dirty state after bus reset. */
+	ret = regcache_sync(rt1320->regmap);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "%s: failed to sync regmap cache: %d\n", __func__, ret);
+
+	ret = regcache_sync(rt1320->mbq_regmap);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "%s: failed to sync mbq regmap cache: %d\n", __func__, ret);
+
 	/* Mark Slave initialization complete */
 	rt1320->first_hw_init = true;
 	rt1320->hw_init = true;
 
+	if (reload_dspfw)
+		schedule_work(&rt1320->load_dspfw_work);
+
 	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&slave->dev);
 
 	dev_dbg(&slave->dev, "%s hw_init complete\n", __func__);
